Q: Add custom messages in assert? A: <p>I agree with the answer to add comments, since you can break at the right line and see it. However, if the application assumes the redirection to log file, custom message could be handy. Here is the macro allowing more flexible output:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>#define ASSERT_M(s,e) if(!(e))std::cout&lt;&lt;s&lt;&lt;&quot;. &quot;;assert(e)

// usage:
int result = 0;
ASSERT_M(&quot;The returned value is &quot; &lt;&lt; result, result == 1);
</code></pre>
<p>The output is:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>
The returned value is 0. Assertion failed: result == 1, file ..., line xxx
</code></pre>
